INT. OFFSHORE OIL RIG CONTROL ROOM - NIGHT

A bank of dim monitors. Rain hammers the porthole. A kettle on a hotplate. The structure creaks.

TOBIAS HALVORSEN-ABIOLA, 40s, rig supervisor, in a grease-stained coverall, reads a gauge. His thumbnail taps the glass. The needle isn't moving.

At the next console, ROSALIE "ROSIE" ENGSTROM, 20s, hard hat on the back of her head, logs numbers on a clipboard. She hums under her breath.

TOBIAS
Rosie. Pressure on well three.

ROSIE
Steady at four-ten.

TOBIAS
It was four-twenty an hour ago.

ROSIE
Sensor drift. It does that.

TOBIAS
Does it?

ROSIE
Sometimes.

He crosses to her console. Looks over her shoulder. She tilts the clipboard toward him.

TOBIAS
Your numbers say four-ten for six hours.

ROSIE
Because it's been four-ten for six hours.

TOBIAS
And the live gauge?

She looks at the screen. Her humming stops.

ROSIE
Four-oh-five.

TOBIAS
Four-oh-five.

ROSIE
It's within tolerance.

TOBIAS
Is it?

COMMS (V.O.)
(crackling)
Control, this is Deck Two. We have a smell down here. Over.

Tobias lifts the handset from its cradle.

TOBIAS
What kind of smell, Deck Two?

COMMS (V.O.)
Like eggs, Toby. Like rotten eggs. Over.

Tobias freezes. Rosie sets the clipboard down very slowly.

ROSIE
Hydrogen sulphide.

TOBIAS
Don't say it.

ROSIE
Toby, that's--

TOBIAS
I know what it is. Don't say it out loud.

He thumbs the handset.

TOBIAS (CONT'D)
Deck Two, evacuate your station. Use the breathing apparatus. Do not run.

COMMS (V.O.)
Copy. Evacuating. Over.

He hangs up. Turns. Rosie is already at the alarm panel, hand over the glass.

ROSIE
Do I pull it?

TOBIAS
Not yet.

ROSIE
Toby!

TOBIAS
If we pull it, a hundred and twenty men run for the lifeboats, and the lifeboats take sixty.

ROSIE
Then we do it in order.

TOBIAS
In order.

He steps to the wall mic. Takes a breath that shakes only a little.

TOBIAS (CONT'D)
(into the mic)
All hands, this is Halvorsen. We have a gas alert on Deck Two. Muster at stations. Walk, do not run. Repeat, walk.

A distant clang. Boots on steel. Voices rising.

ROSIE
You said "walk."

TOBIAS
They'll walk fast.

ROSIE
Toby, the gauge.

He looks. The needle on well three leaps, quivers, and plunges.

TOBIAS
Pull it.

She smashes the glass and pulls the lever.

Sirens howl through the whole structure. The lights go red.

TOBIAS (CONT'D)
(not loud, to himself)
Please let the lines hold.

ROSIE
They'll hold.

TOBIAS
How do you know?

ROSIE
Because I checked them this morning.

He closes his eyes for one second. Opens them. Grabs the clipboard, her pen, her sleeve.

TOBIAS
Come on.

They run into the red corridor.
